speechtext:
1. $431,454.99 as shown in answer to question No. 733 on April 22, 1964 (Hansard, page 2452.)

2. (a) Provision for such repayment is contained in vote 106e, supplementary estimates "E", 1963-64 in the total amount of $225,000 and it is expected that disbursements will shortly be made from this vote.
(b) Precise details cannot be provided since claims have not yet been verified for payment. It is expected that expenditures of the following order will be involved:
(i)	for the redemption, with interest, of commercial bank loans made after consultation with the previous government to the Dawson city festival foundation, $152,000;
(ii)	to meet in full verified trade accounts, $28,000;
(iii)	to meet in part other claims against the Dawson city festival foundation, $45,000.
